From: Yaagl DX12 P3 rebase <yaagl-dx12@local>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wine-p3: ZZZ compatibility (ws2_32 timeout + mfreadwrite CW #20833)

Provenance
==========
- Timeout: forward-port of dwproton/gi-timeout
  0009-HACK-ws2_32-Allow-changing-request-timeout-with-WINE.patch
  mirrored at riverfog7/macports-wine@098941d867f8793f559035e298ceb69a8e69f1f3
  (authors: teapot4195 / NelloKudo / Lily).
- MF: forward-port of Yaagl/macports
  mf/0003-mfreadwrite-reader-Rely-on-the-video-processor-sampl.patch
  (Rémi Bernon; CW-Bug-Id: #20833), same mirror pin.

Target tree
===========
- Upstream Wine 11.17 working tree at build/wine-p3/source
  (git describe/HEAD: 913e31f201d344223bdf3d13a50a41af35893d12).

Scope
=====
- dlls/ws2_32/socket.c only for WINE_ENABLE_TIMEOUT_FIX.
- dlls/mfreadwrite/reader.c only for the justified cutscene path hack.
- Explicitly excluded: ntdll/win32u/winemac, launch wrapper, CN/crypt32,
  ntoskrnl/wdfldr driver stubs, full Proton media stack.

Timeout contract (failure behavior)
===================================
- Active only when getenv("WINE_ENABLE_TIMEOUT_FIX") is non-zero AND the
  process image basename is GenshinImpact.exe / YuanShen.exe /
  ZenlessZoneZero.exe (cached after first probe).
- Hook runs from WSACreateEvent; at most two heap scans per process.
- Scans the process heap for busy blocks starting with magic
  AD DB DE C0 and, if the block is large enough, writes eight bytes
  {0x60,0xea,0x00,0x00,0x60,0xea,0x00,0x00} (= 0x0000ea60 / 60000ms x2)
  at undocumented offset 0x2f8.
- Safety retained/added vs published patch:
  * NULL ImagePathName.Buffer => cache miss / no-op
  * HeapLock failure => no-op
  * NULL entry.lpData skipped
  * write requires cbData >= 0x2f8 + sizeof(timeout_buf) (not merely 0x300)
- Undocumented magic/offset are intentionally NOT redesigned; game-version
  layout drift remains a runtime uncertainty.
- If magic is absent or size check fails: silent no-op (login/timeout
  symptoms may persist). TRACE previously said "5000ms" but the bytes are
  60000ms; TRACE text corrected here without changing bytes.

MF decision
===========
- Published Yaagl media patch is NOT upstreamed: Wine 11.17 still has the
  reader-side IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx path (recently touched in-tree).
- Stock Portfile for the public Yaagl overlay still applies this patch.
- This repo's installMediaFoundation() only runs for bh3/cbjq channels;
  ZZZ/nap therefore relies on builtin mfreadwrite, so the wine-side patch
  remains the minimum justified cutscene carry (not native MF cab install,
  not full Proton media).
- Forward-port keeps MFUnlockWorkQueue on reader release. The published
  macports patch context accidentally deleted that call; restoring it is
  required for work-queue lifetime correctness and is not a behavior change
  to the allocator removal intent.

Uncertainties requiring runtime smoke
=====================================
- Heap magic/offset still match current ZenlessZoneZero.exe curl objects.
- Cutscenes still play on builtin MF after allocator removal on 11.17.
- No OS ZZZ import evidence found for CN/crypt32 or ntoskrnl stubs.

